{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773436896,"nonce":"i5GuH22uvmUtyvvNCSOy9bCZ5o4=","title":"Chat tab: first-class agent sessions + unified chat/history rendering","message":"## Problem\nThe Chat tab currently treats rich view and terminal as two equivalent views over the same session, but rich view depends on transport assumptions that do not hold in practice. In Claude interactive mode, prompts submitted from rich view can succeed in the terminal while rich view remains stuck on a synthetic user bubble plus a generic streaming indicator. History is ingested and stored successfully, but the detail rendering reads like a debug ledger rather than a coherent chat transcript.\n\n## Context\nThe desired product direction is now explicit: agent chat sessions should be first-class, with terminal as an alternative or debug fallback rather than the primary transport contract. Provider-native logs should remain the main ingestion source for History so chats run outside Mandible still appear there, but Chat and History should converge on a shared normalized render model and a similar visual language.\n\n## Scope\n- Make chat sessions primary and terminal secondary/debug\n- Replace PTY-scraped rich streaming assumptions with a proper live chat event path\n- Unify Chat and History rendering around grouped turns/messages while preserving per-event selection\n- Improve History whitespace and block presentation so it resembles a chat UI rather than a flat event dump\n- Verify ingestion/update behavior remains incremental when provider logs gain new turns\n\n## Notes\nRelated existing issues cover earlier transport bugs and framework generalization, but this issue tracks the integrated product change.\n\n---\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}